# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
# An Unfold refused by a fillet on a surface edge, its message in words
# (mitcad#1942; docs/ui-conventions.md "What a message says"), on
# sheet-unfold-fillet.json (the sheet F3.b0 with Fillet1 F4 on its back
# edge y = 20, a Flange F5 and SheetUnfold1 F6 of its bend, failed):
#   1. SheetUnfold1 edited from the timeline: the panel says why in words,
#      the fillet by its name and what it does, with no feature id and no
#      "panel ... slot".
#   2. Esc cancels the command.
# Run by tools/ui-sheet-unfold-fillet-test.sh (Linux),
# tools/ui-windows-sheet-unfold-fillet-test.ps1 (Windows) and
# tools/ui-macos-sheet-unfold-fillet-test.sh (macOS).
expect-ever 'View area'
wait-idle
key F6
wait-idle
expect-ever '^Timeline SheetUnfold1 at '

# 1. Edited: the refusal in words.
mark
dblclick-logged '^Timeline SheetUnfold1 at '
wait-log '^Editing F6 with Unfold$'
wait-log '^Panel Unfold error: sheet Unfold needs the sheet.s developed form, but Fillet1 rounds edges of the sheet.s faces, which cannot be flattened; only corners through the thickness unfold$' 30
wait-idle
expect-no-log '^Panel Unfold error: .*(F[0-9]|slot [0-9])'

# 2. Esc cancels.
mark
key Escape
wait-log '^Command Unfold cancelled$'
wait-idle
